The system is a Role-based Access Control (RBAC) system operating in a multi-user environment, supporting role hierarchy, temporary role delegation, revocation of delegated roles, and concurrent request processing. The system ensures authorization correctness, delegation and permission consistency, liveness of request processing, and safety under concurrency. Users are assigned security clearance levels and may submit requests within their clearance constraints. An Emergency Module is to be integrated, allowing for emergency protocols that alter normal operations temporarily.

PROSPECTIVE FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
=======================
R1: Triggering Emergency Mode
Exactly two administrators are required to trigger an emergency, which causes the system to enter Emergency mode.

