R1: Triggering Emergency Mode
Exactly two administrators are required to trigger an emergency, which causes the system to enter Emergency mode.

R2: Duration of Emergency Mode
Emergency mode is active for a limited time and must eventually return to Normal mode. It can also be manually deactivated early by exactly two administrators.

R3: Behavior During Emergency Mode
R3.1: Request Processing
During Emergency mode, request processing may bypass the FIFO order to prioritize high classification requests.

R3.2: Role Exclusivity
Users may temporarily hold mutually exclusive roles.

R3.3: Emergency Privileges
Administrators temporarily hold emergency privileges.

R4: Post-Emergency Mode Cleanup
R4.1: Revocation of Emergency Privileges
All emergency privileges must be revoked after Emergency mode ends.

R4.2: Revocation of Delegated Roles
All roles delegated during the emergency must be revoked.

R4.3: Credential Update
Administrators must update their credentials after Emergency mode ends.
```

