SYSTEM OVERVIEW
===============
The system is a Role-based Access Control (RBAC) system operating in a multi-user environment, supporting role hierarchy, temporary role delegation, revocation of delegated roles, and concurrent request processing. The system ensures authorization correctness, delegation and permission consistency, liveness of request processing, and safety under concurrency. Users are assigned security clearance levels and may submit requests within their clearance constraints. An Emergency Module is to be integrated, allowing for emergency protocols that alter normal operations temporarily, with manual deactivation by two administrators if needed.

EXISTING-SYSTEM ASSUMPTIONS AND CONSTRAINTS
============================================
- Users can only submit requests within their security clearance level.
- Delegated roles must meet the delegate's minimum clearance requirement.
- Requests are processed concurrently in FIFO order unless in Emergency mode.
- Emergency mode requires exactly two administrators to initiate.
- Emergency mode must eventually end, returning the system to Normal mode, either through timeout or manual deactivation by two administrators.

PROSPECTIVE FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
====================================
R1: Triggering Emergency Mode
Exactly two administrators are required to trigger an emergency, which causes the system to enter Emergency mode.

R2: Duration of Emergency Mode
Emergency mode is active for a limited time and must eventually return to Normal mode. It can also be manually deactivated early by two administrators.

R3: Behavior During Emergency Mode
R3.1: Request Processing
During Emergency mode, request processing may bypass the FIFO order to prioritize high classification requests.

R3.2: Role Exclusivity
Users may temporarily hold mutually exclusive roles.

R3.3: Emergency Privileges
Administrators temporarily hold emergency privileges.

R4: Post-Emergency Mode Cleanup
R4.1: Revocation of Emergency Privileges
All emergency privileges must be revoked after Emergency mode ends.

R4.2: Revocation of Delegated Roles
All roles delegated during the emergency must be revoked.

R4.3: Credential Update
Administrators must update their credentials after Emergency mode ends.
